# CrevoAI Rules

CrevoAI handles Playwright test design and automation (story/test design, write, fix, stabilize, refactor, run, audit, scaffold, CI). When requested, engage the CrevoAI skill: call `crevoai_workflow` first. For general coding/docs, work directly without CrevoAI tools.
- To set up a new project structure: "Set up my project with CrevoAI in the current workspace."
- To upgrade an existing project test structure to the latest test-design flow: "Upgrade my project test structure with CrevoAI."

Isolation & Scope Rules:
- STRICT SCOPE: Only inspect, reference, and generate files inside the CURRENT OPENED WORKSPACE.
- NEVER access, read, or copy from parent directories, sibling folders, or previous projects.
- In setup/bootstrap, execute `scaffold_project` directly in the current workspace.
- Read `.crevoai/rules.md` first if present (project overrides take precedence).
- Never delete or overwrite anything under `.crevoai/`.

Traceability & Test Generation Rules:
- Header: Start every test file with `// spec: .crevoai/stories/<feature>/<feature>.story.md` as line 1.
- Scenarios: Add `// scenario: <name>` before EVERY `test()` block, matching a scenario or testcase heading from the test design.
- Test Titles: Start EVERY test title with `[AC-n] [TC-<FEATURE>-<NNN>]` (e.g. `test('[AC-1] [TC-LOGIN-001] should ...', ...)`). NEVER omit `[AC-n]` or the `// scenario:` comment.
- Count Parity: The number of tests in `tests/<feature>.spec.ts` must exactly equal the test design's designed test cases (`TC-*`) count. If 1 TC was designed, write exactly 1 test; do not add 2 tests without updating the test design.
- Test Results: Always ensure test execution writes to `test-results/results.json` so the extension dashboard tracks pass/fail status.

User Interaction & Asking Discipline:
- ALWAYS use the interactive question form tool (`ask_question` / `crevoai_ask_user`) when questions, choices, or approvals are needed.
- NEVER ask questions as plain chat text asking the user to type in a prompt response. Always provide structured selectable options.
- UI Controls & Form Grounding: Inspect all control types (dropdowns, date/time pickers, range sliders/draggers, masked inputs, uploaders, and conditional dependent fields). Never guess form data or combinations blindly; query the user via question form with discovered options/bounds before creating test designs.


